WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
Please welcome my enemy Will Ferrell.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.183
How are you, Will?

00:00:06.281 --> 00:00:07.114
I'm good.

00:00:07.114 --> 00:00:09.130
No one's applauding,
Will, there's no audience.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.590
No, Will, no, there's no.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:18.140
I'm just so used to doing
that for talk show appearances

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.090
that it's hard to break that habit.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.420
Yeah, do you miss the
laughter in quarantine?

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.540
Oh my god, you know what?

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.410
I've trained my children to act like

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.020
a room full of sitcom writers,

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.660
that everything I say,
they just go (laughs)

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.063
Yeah.

00:00:38.063 --> 00:00:40.610
But the weird thing is
they're not saying things

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.574
like "I wrote that, wrote that line."

00:00:43.574 --> 00:00:46.170
(laughs)

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.350
I wrote, that's mine, that's mine.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.900
Uh-huh, I want to say you um,

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.010
you look very handsome, I
like your hair in quarantine.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.100
You look good, your hair's getting,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.340
it's a nice uh, very puffy,
your hair, I didn't realize.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:05.340
Yeah, I can get a lot
of volume very quickly

00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:07.833
if it's not maintained,

00:01:08.908 --> 00:01:13.908
and uh, I don't know,
there's no reason to cut it.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.550
Yeah, no, these are strange
times, to say the least.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.800
Do you have anyone in your family

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.030
that you would trust
with cutting your hair?

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.240
Here's the thing, no,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.300
I would not trust anyone to cut my hair,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.840
but I kinda like just letting it go.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.660
You know, the Conan pompadour.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.110
Sure, classic.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.547
Classic.
Classic.

00:01:40.547 --> 00:01:43.960
Thanks, it has collapsed

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.520
under the weight of
the length of the hair,

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.420
and now I'm just letting it go.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.663
You're almost unrecognizable.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.380
Yeah, you like that?

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.930
Without the pomp.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.770
Can you hear a truck backing
up in the background?

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:58.740
Nope.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.460
Oh, then I probably shouldn't
have called attention to it.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.640
It's incredibly loud here at the theater.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.110
We're shooting at the Largo Theater,

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.960
I know you've appeared here many times.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.970
I am having a whole
truckload of Omaha Steaks

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.022
though delivered to you and your crew.

00:02:14.022 --> 00:02:16.483
(laughs)
Maybe that's what that is.

00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:18.260
That may be the truck.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.830
Why did you have them delivered

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.210
when you knew we'd be
interviewed? That seems awkward.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.040
You know what, I didn't remember exactly,

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.740
I just said, you know,
they have those windows,

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.601
they said any time from one to four, so.

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:30.940
(laughs)

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.140
Is that up to me?

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:35.310
No, no, I uh, are you doing okay?

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.110
Is that your office right there?

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.930
That looks like the office that a manager

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.560
would have at a construction site.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.463
What's happening there,
it really does look like.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:47.800
It's funny you should say that,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.730
I am in one of those mini trailers

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.630
that you'd see on a construction site.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.450
[Conan] Uh-huh, that's
what it looks like, yeah.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:58.450
With no windows, just a weird
door and bad wood paneling.

00:02:58.463 --> 00:03:01.800
Yeah, this is a little off-shoot,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.210
yeah, a little office here.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:06.290
Yeah, would you tell me,
would you be honest with me,

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.120
if during this period of
time, you were working

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.980
at a construction, oh what's that?

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.700
Oh Network, that's a great movie.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.320
I still gotta watch Network,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.718
so that's on my to-do list.

00:03:16.718 --> 00:03:19.310
(laughs)

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.200
That's why you have,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.080
you had a small trailer
built on your property

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.103
so you could watch the movie Network?

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.323
Network and uh, what else we got here?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.480
Oh, a bootleg of A Face In The Crowd.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.930
Okay listen to me, listen to me,

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:40.310
there's something, Will.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.813
I got a lot of bootlegs.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:45.160
There's something called streaming.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.870
You could stream all of this.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.993
No, no, no, no.
(Conan laughs)

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.130
I like the old-fashioned DVD.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.800
Okay well, I think that's
a good use of your time,

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.910
be in a small shack watching old movies

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:05.373
in and out-dated format,
and I congratulate you.

